{"journal_version":1,"sequence":10,"replace_from":15,"message_count":16,"messages":[{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"Verification passed. One consideration: should search state live in App so that the count? Not needed. Also the \"Clear search\" button's accessible name — text content is \"Clear search\", fine.\n\nRisk: after clearing, button remains until blur; if a hidden test asserts button count/hidden when empty, it could conflict, but the focus requirement requires persistence.\n\nAlso consider: after clearing while focus stays on button, pressing Tab moves on. Fine.\n\nDone. Report.","content":"Change made in `src/components/TaskList.tsx` (only file touched):\n- Added a local `query` state and a `type=\"search\"` input with `aria-label=\"Search tasks\"` above the list.\n- Filtering is immediate and case-insensitive over task titles (`toLowerCase().includes`), computed as `visibleTasks`; selection state remains in `App`, so hiding a row never clears the selected task and the detail card is unaffected.\n- A non-empty query renders a `Clear search` button. Clearing resets the query, restores all tasks, and the button stays mounted while it holds focus (tracked via `keepClearVisible`, released on blur or on the next input change), so focus remains on that button after clearing.\n- When nothing matches, the list is replaced by exactly `No tasks match your search.`; the existing `ul.task-list` markup, selected-row class, select and edit handlers are unchanged.\n\nExact command run (via `verify_frontend`):\n- `npm run verify:agent` → `npm run build && npm run test:public` (tsc, vite build, 6 Playwright tests) — exit 0, all 6 passed.\n\nRemaining risks:\n- No new automated coverage for the search interaction was added (existing public tests untouched); behavior was validated only by build/type-check and the existing suite.\n- The `Clear search` button intentionally persists briefly after clearing (until blur) to satisfy the focus requirement; a future check expecting it to disappear instantly on an empty query would need re-review.\n- New classes (`task-search`, `task-search-input`, `task-list-panel`, `task-empty`) have no dedicated CSS yet, so the control uses default input/button styling.","response_items":[{"id":"e8929bb1-e5b6-42b2-b467-e1bb2a04d2ae","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"Verification passed. One consideration: should search state live in App so that the count? Not needed. Also the \"Clear search\" button's accessible name — text content is \"Clear search\", fine.\n\nRisk: after clearing, button remains until blur; if a hidden test asserts button count/hidden when empty, it could conflict, but the focus requirement requires persistence.\n\nAlso consider: after clearing while focus stays on button, pressing Tab moves on. Fine.\n\nDone. Report.","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":"c8078ae1-e826-4326-a098-169803ff1275-0","status":"completed"},{"id":"c13255d2-dda3-4065-b85c-7132c7a32d47","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"Change made in `src/components/TaskList.tsx` (only file touched):\n- Added a local `query` state and a `type=\"search\"` input with `aria-label=\"Search tasks\"` above the list.\n- Filtering is immediate and case-insensitive over task titles (`toLowerCase().includes`), computed as `visibleTasks`; selection state remains in `App`, so hiding a row never clears the selected task and the detail card is unaffected.\n- A non-empty query renders a `Clear search` button. Clearing resets the query, restores all tasks, and the button stays mounted while it holds focus (tracked via `keepClearVisible`, released on blur or on the next input change), so focus remains on that button after clearing.\n- When nothing matches, the list is replaced by exactly `No tasks match your search.`; the existing `ul.task-list` markup, selected-row class, select and edit handlers are unchanged.\n\nExact command run (via `verify_frontend`):\n- `npm run verify:agent` → `npm run build && npm run test:public` (tsc, vite build, 6 Playwright tests) — exit 0, all 6 passed.\n\nRemaining risks:\n- No new automated coverage for the search interaction was added (existing public tests untouched); behavior was validated only by build/type-check and the existing suite.\n- The `Clear search` button intentionally persists briefly after clearing (until blur) to satisfy the focus requirement; a future check expecting it to disappear instantly on an empty query would need re-review.\n- New classes (`task-search`, `task-search-input`, `task-list-panel`, `task-empty`) have no dedicated CSS yet, so the control uses default input/button styling.","type":"output_text","logprobs":[]}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":"final_answer"}],"timestamp":"2026-11-22T15:53:20.905695+00:00"}],"meta":{"snapshot_version":1,"aid":0,"role":"workflow_agent","model":"deepseek-flash","session_state":{"used_tokens":24642,"context_tokens":5944,"step_count":6,"markup_recovered":0,"recent_call_hashes":["f050299d2355e4fa645cfbfdaa86637a","22c5ff12f36f01d15d042e587aa72016","09c561a451cdcb895ea6db3f6e9aa484","73d921794b476d3d493a2e4b82923490","9ca637a1c2eb92c23a06d776d6d37478","dff780a8fd193f09e2e8edcfcdd1a2ad","00315bdf9e34380f13946d97f176140b","3c45d71dcb1acaddc13d0e86e5418077"],"reads_since_last_edit":0,"has_landed_write":true,"low_yield_since_progress":0,"distinct_evidence_count":8,"scout_ledger":[{"tool":"file_read","target":"src/components/TaskList.tsx","outcome":"hit","snippet":"File: src/components/TaskList.tsx (32 lines total, showing 1-32) 1 import type { Task } from '../types'; 2 3 type Props = { 4 tasks: Task[]; 5 selectedId: number; 6 onSelect: (id: number) => void; 7 onEdit: (id: number) => void; 8 }; 9 10 e"},{"tool":"file_read","target":"src/App.tsx","outcome":"hit","snippet":"File: src/App.tsx (90 lines total, showing 1-90) 1 import { useState } from 'react'; 2 import { AsyncPanel } from './components/AsyncPanel'; 3 import { NewTaskForm } from './compon